      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Nalma was one of Tasinar's branded slaves. Her husband had been sold to a different slaver, and she hoped to find him. Kaladin promised to help, and led her and several other slaves in an escape. They hid in the wilderness for five days before Tasinar's hunters closed in.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "55" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "97" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As they moved through the underbrush, Nalma's leg was caught in a steel trap. She told Kaladin to run, but he stayed and tried to bandage the wound, holding her hand as she bled to death. Her screams drew the hunters, who killed the other runaways and let only Kaladin live.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "55" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "97" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Remembered",
